// EXPECTED TO FAIL: a multi-arm block whose conditions leave a GAP, with no `totality:`.
//
// The arms condition on `n = ZERO` and `less_than(ONE, n)`, which say nothing whatever about
// `n = ONE`. So `f(ONE)` is UNDETERMINED: no arm's condition holds there, and the block
// constrains it not at all. Not unsound -- an `oper` is total, so the term denotes something --
// but underdetermined, which is exactly what a definition exists to rule out and an axiom
// exists to disclose. A reader sees a definition block and concludes the symbol is pinned down.
//
// `consistency:` cannot catch this. The two conditions are DISJOINT, so every clause pair is
// vacuously consistent -- the block is perfectly consistent and perfectly incomplete.
//
// THE INSTANCE THAT MOTIVATED THE CHECK: `std/ring/polynomial.b4m`'s `monus` (truncated
// subtraction, formerly `theGapTo`) was written with only `monus(i, ZERO) = i` and a
// `succ`/`succ` step arm, so `i < j` matched NEITHER clause and the symbol was undetermined
// exactly where the flooring was the whole point. The declaration's own comment claimed a floor
// clause that had never been written, and nothing flagged it for sessions.
sort Nat
const ZERO: Nat
const ONE: Nat
oper succ(n: Nat) => Nat
pred less_than(a: Nat, b: Nat)

oper f(n: Nat) => Nat:
  f(n) = ZERO when n = ZERO;
  f(n) = succ(n) when less_than(ONE, n).
  consistency: _
